      "shortDescription": "Nakanishi Jaeger develops and manufactures high-frequency spindle systems and compact electric drives in Germany. The official portfolio covers cylindrical, flange, dressing, block-housing and dental spindles together with synchronous, asynchronous and application-specific motors.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Nakanishi Jaeger GmbH is the current company behind the former Alfred Jäger spindle business. Official company information identifies the operation in Ober-Mörlen, Germany, and states that Jaeger and its subsidiaries have been part of the NSK NAKANISHI Group since 1 January 2023. The company develops and manufactures spindle systems and motors, with development and production activities carried out in Germany.",
        "The documented spindle range includes Z-Line cylindrical spindles, F-Line flange designs, ARS-Line dressing spindles, Block-Line housings, Chopper systems, DentaDrive dental spindles and synchronous-motor Power-Line units. Nakanishi Jaeger also develops synchronous and asynchronous motors for spindle drives, pumps, automation, e-mobility, turbo compressors and generators. Published spindle applications include deburring, dental machining, die and mould work, engraving, grinding, printed-circuit-board processing and robotic machining. Official downloads provide product catalogues and supporting technical documentation."
      ],
