      "foundedYear": 1972,
      "parentCompany": null,
      "shortDescription": "Autoflame Engineering designs and manufactures combustion-management controls for industrial and commercial boilers and burners. Its systems combine fuel-air ratio control, flame safeguards, emissions analysis, boiler-room monitoring, water-level management, servomotors, valves and sensing components.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Autoflame Engineering Ltd. is a British manufacturer of combustion-management technology for industrial and commercial boiler and burner applications. The business began with oil and gas firing work in the late 1960s and was officially incorporated in 1972. Its corporate and manufacturing headquarters are in Biggin Hill, Kent, where the company develops and manufactures its control products.",
        "The current range includes Mini Mk9 MM, Mk8 MM and Mini Mk8 MM burner and boiler controllers, Mk8 EGA Evo exhaust-gas analysis and trim systems, and the Mk8 DTI interface for boiler-room monitoring. Autoflame also documents servomotors, control valves, UV and IR flame scanners, pressure and temperature sensors, water-level probes, blowdown controls and related modules. The systems are designed for steam and hot-water boilers, kilns and steam generators and support burner control, flame supervision, emissions monitoring, data acquisition and integrated boiler-room management."
      ],
