      "statusModifier": "ACQUIRED_BRAND",
      "shortDescription": "Balston is a Parker brand for industrial filtration, air drying and gas-generation equipment. The official range includes compressed-air and gas filters, sample filters, filter housings and elements, air dryers, and generators for nitrogen, hydrogen, zero air and analytical gases.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Balston began as Balston Inc. in the United States in 1970, manufacturing a coalescing-filter design, and introduced a laboratory gas generator in 1979. An official Parker history document records Parker Hannifin's acquisition of Balston in 2000. The brand now forms part of Parker's Industrial Gas Filtration and Generation business and remains identified on current Parker products and technical literature.",
        "The documented portfolio covers 2000 Series and 6000 Series compressed-air filters, sterile-air systems, ASME vessels, gas and liquid sample-analyser filters, disposable filter and adsorption units, replacement elements and membrane air dryers. Parker also publishes Balston nitrogen, hydrogen, zero-air and TOC gas generators for industrial, food and beverage, life-science, process, marine, power-generation and analytical-laboratory applications. The official filtration and air-drying catalogue provides selection and maintenance information for these systems."
      ],
